---
title: Advanced API
description: Scheduler helpers and namespaced user context exports.
---

## Entrypoints

| Entrypoint | Additional exports |
| --- | --- |
| `spektral/advanced` | Framework-neutral core plus scheduler helpers |
| `/svelte/advanced`, `/vue/advanced` | Adapter runtime, scheduler helpers, user-context read/write API |
| `/react/advanced` | Same, plus `useSetSpektralUserContext` |

## Scheduler helpers

```ts
applySchedulerPreset(
	scheduler,
	preset: 'performance' | 'balanced' | 'debug',
	overrides?
): SchedulerPresetConfig
```

| Preset | Diagnostics/profiling | Window |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `performance` | Off | 60 |
| `balanced` | On | 120 |
| `debug` | On | 240 |

Overrides may set `diagnosticsEnabled`, `profilingEnabled`, and `profilingWindow`. The window must be a safe integer from 1 through 10,000. Diagnostics and profiling currently share state, so both boolean overrides must match.

`captureSchedulerDebugSnapshot(scheduler)` returns enable flags, window, resolved schedule, last-run timings, and rolling profiling snapshot.

## User context

Advanced adapter entrypoints export `useSpektralUserContext`, `setSpektralUserContext`, their types, and scheduler helpers. React adds `useSetSpektralUserContext` for hook-bound writes.

See [User Context](/docs/user-context) and [Hooks API](/docs/api-hooks-reference#advanced-user-context).
